Sval: console messages say where they came from, with filters by origin

Each Web Console and Browser Console message gets a label for the page's
own scripts, an extension, or Sval itself, an extension script's source
link names its extension, and the filter bar gets Page, Extensions and Sval
toggles and a one-extension menu. The logic is in Sval's added files
(browser/components/sval/console-origin*.js), which the console requires by
their chrome:// URLs; this has prepareMessage give each message's frame its
origin, and wires the label, the filters' state and the visibility check
into the console. The console's components, reducers and filter state are
Mozilla's, and no chrome API reaches them.

